# M1 showcase, part 2 of 2: the same highest range at vertical scale 1/8,
# which Andrew is still considering. Run in its own world:
#
#   --vscale 0.125 --height 4096 --sea-level 2048 --n 131072
#
# (scripts/showcase.py runs it). At 1/8 the range climbs from ~600 m at lon
# 112.5 over a 1.0-1.1 km shoulder at lon 114-115 to a 1.65 km crest at lon
# 117.25 (T2: the ranges are real now, and the old keys at 850-1360 m ran
# inside them); the flight comes in low from the west and climbs over the
# flank, golden hour behind it, 200-300 m over the ground all the way.
mode fly
at 69.2 117.0 1900
sun 5
at 69.2 112.5 800
look 90 -4
recmode settle
hud off
record 50_vscale8.mp4 30
caption Vertical scale 1/8 (under consideration): the same highest range
key 2.5 69.2 115.0 1250 92 -5
key 5.0 69.2 117.0 1750 92 -6
key 7.5 69.2 119.0 1850 95 -7
key 9.5 69.2 120.6 1850 98 -8
fly
stop
